codex
The fresh proof does print `#Top` with exit 0, but the semantics smoke test has exposed a material defect the candidate logs missed: on the required empty-string boundary, LLVM execution aborts in `substrString` instead of returning Python’s `"No"`. The `exec(If(...))` encoding evaluates both branches, so an unreachable later subscript is nevertheless forced. I’m correcting only my result-parser bug and rerunning the concrete comparison to isolate this candidate defect cleanly.
